+- finding-source · {"version":1,"source":"roast-code/round-1","artifact":"docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart-roast-pr-1.md","kind":"roast","verdict":"Should-fix (4 confirmed) [panel-capped: 21 unverified]","occurrences":[{"section":"Confirmed findings","position":1,"key":"[Should-fix] src/ports/threads.rs:179; src/daemon/compose.rs:1031","text":"[Should-fix] src/ports/threads.rs:179; src/daemon/compose.rs:1031 \u2014 Every local ThreadsError::Rejected (namespace guard's retryable stale-snapshot error, host claim, intent-dir) is mapped to the definitive refusal InvalidRequest, so the restart rebind is never retried in that incarnation and the resurrect is parked until replace or the pane changes. [lanes: correctness, premortem, api-contract, testing]\n  verdict: confirmed (reproduce \u2713 / refute \u2717-survived / ground \u2713)\n  evidence: src/ports/threads.rs `from_error` maps `ThreadsError::Rejected(_)` to `SeatRestoreRefusal::InvalidRequest`, which is not in `retryable()`. src/daemon/compose.rs `Endpoint::guard` maps every namespace guard io error to `Rejected`, including namespace.rs:136-144 \"stale external call snapshot; retry from the current committed namespace\". src/threads/effects.rs `rebind_held_seat` (~1919) writes `rebind_refused:<clone>` on a non-retryable refusal, and `rebindable()` (line 553) then plans no rebind for the rest of the incarnation. Design 4.2 lists \"error, timeout, threads unreachable\" as transient and retried every pass. All three seats confirmed at head 7d9f495; `from_error` is new in this diff.\n  fix-shape hint: Map graph-local `Rejected` errors (guard, host, intent dir, `MutateError::Local`) to a retryable refusal, and add a fault-injection test; `restore_outcome_maps_every_variant` currently pins the wrong mapping."},{"section":"Confirmed findings","position":2,"key":"[Should-fix] CHANGELOG.md:24","text":"[Should-fix] CHANGELOG.md:24 \u2014 The user-facing docs and the error/doctor text promise that every herdr-threads daemon older than 3.6.0 refuses graph's service_session_v4 by name, but v3.5.0 already serves service_session_v4, so a 3.5.x daemon registers silently and the documented upgrade guidance never fires. [lanes: hygiene-docs]\n  verdict: confirmed (reproduce \u2713 / refute \u2717-survived / ground \u2713)\n  evidence: In the pinned submodule, `git show v3.5.0:src/protocol/service.rs` line 30 defines `SERVICE_SESSION_CAPABILITY_V4 = \"service_session_v4\"` and line 42 `V4`. CHANGELOG.md:24 says \"A daemon older than 3.6.0 refuses it\"; README.md:239 says the same. src/daemon/doctor.rs:114 emits the upgrade step only when a refusal contains `service_session_v4`, which never happens on 3.5.x. On 3.5.x the 3.6.0-only held-seat rebind degrades to `rebind_refused` / `clones.restart_held` with no upgrade hint. The PR's own reviews/inv-1/final-review-inv-1.md lists this under \"Must fix before landing\"; head 7d9f495 only adds docs.\n  fix-shape hint: Either correct the docs and doctor text to name 3.5.x as the exception, or add a real daemon version guard (or map the 3.5.x rebind refusal to the named upgrade error)."},{"section":"Confirmed findings","position":3,"key":"[Nit] src/model/clone.rs:100; src/model/clone.rs:107","text":"[Nit] src/model/clone.rs:100; src/model/clone.rs:107 \u2014 The serde default keyed=true for legacy Retired seat facts misreads keyless reversible facts written by the old graph against an already-upgraded threads daemon (the documented upgrade order), routing undo to UnretireSeat instead of ResurrectSeat and suppressing the preview note. [lanes: data-migrations, deploy-safety, api-contract]\n  verdict: confirmed (reproduce \u2713 / refute \u2717-survived \u2014 refute seat voted REJECT as immaterial, outvoted 2-1 / ground \u2713)\n  evidence: src/model/clone.rs:100-107 defaults a missing `keyed` to true, on the premise that legacy facts came from threads 3.1.0. CHANGELOG.md:29 requires the daemon at 3.6.0 before graph is upgraded. Base src/threads/mapping.rs:166-171 maps `retirement_state: Some(Reversible)` to Reversible without consulting the key, so the old graph on an upgraded daemon persists `Retired{reversible:true}` for a closed keyless seat. After the upgrade, `unretirable()` (effects.rs:652-675) fires and `resurrectable()` does not; preview.rs `seat_window_note` returns None. The refute seat accepts the mechanism and rejects only on materiality: `fact_needs_write` rewrites the fact on the next successful read, so the cost is one wrong UnretireSeat attempt and a missing preview note. Both confirming seats rate it Nit for the same reason. Not verified by any seat: how threads 3.6.0 answers UnretireSeat for a keyless seat.\n  fix-shape hint: Derive the legacy default from `CloneRecord.keyless` instead of a constant true, or state the window in the Migration section."},{"section":"Confirmed findings","position":4,"key":"[Nit] src/threads/adapter.rs:272; src/threads/adapter.rs:467","text":"[Nit] src/threads/adapter.rs:272; src/threads/adapter.rs:467 \u2014 Rolling graph back while a ResurrectSeat intent is pending breaks the older binary's threads adapter at construction, because herdr-threads 3.1.0 cannot deserialize the intent file; the migration notes do not mention it. [lanes: data-migrations, deploy-safety]\n  verdict: confirmed (reproduce \u2713 / refute \u2717-survived \u2014 refute seat voted REJECT as out of the stated downgrade scope, outvoted 2-1 / ground \u2713)\n  evidence: Head src/threads/adapter.rs:271-272 calls `ServiceIntentJournal::open` then `journal.pending()?` in `ServiceThreads::new`. At the base pin 482e0d2, herdr-threads src/client/service.rs:364-372 `pending()` runs `serde_json::from_slice::<SavedServiceIntent>` on every `*.intent` file and propagates errors; `ServiceOperation` (protocol/service.rs:194-195) has no `ResurrectSeat` variant. An older graph binary therefore fails adapter construction until the pending intent file is removed. CHANGELOG Migration (lines 29-31) does not mention the intent journal. The refute seat's point, that the v0.3.0 notes already say \"downgrade is not supported\", is acknowledged by both confirming seats, which is why they rate it Nit.\n  fix-shape hint: Add one Migration line: before rolling graph back, delete pending `*.intent` files under `.graph-local/threads-intents`."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":1,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:536","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:536 \u2014 The 'incarnation' that gates the rebind want and the restart_held status has no time bound: any seat that reads Unresolved at any point after the last Herdr restart (days or weeks later, including ContinuityStatus::Remote and Resolved-without-target, which mapping.rs also maps to Unresolved) is treated as restart-held \u2014 graph fires a ResurrectSeat rebind at it, records a definitive refusal, and after 90 s shows a clones.restart_held row and doctor WARN telling the operator to run an operator rebind."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":2,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/daemon/compose.rs:870","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/daemon/compose.rs:870 \u2014 ServiceThreads construction now depends on resolving the Herdr host locator (canonicalizing the Herdr socket's parent directory), so if that directory is absent when the slot is (re)built \u2014 plausibly during the very Herdr restart this feature targets \u2014 every threads operation, not just resurrect/rebind, fails with Rejected (terminal Failed for ordinary effects, definitive refusal for rebind/resurrect)."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":3,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/reconcile/herdr_exec.rs:607","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/reconcile/herdr_exec.rs:607 \u2014 When a keyless clone's undo-restore StartAgent loses its response (deadline missed, effect status Unknown), the retry path records the `launched:` meta unconditionally, so the hg-lnw.3 fix (no launch record for a keyless restore launch) is bypassed and the ordinary exited-agent relaunch is shut out for that clone for good."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":4,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:2616","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:2616 \u2014 A membership poll effect that executes after `AcknowledgeResurrected` overwrites the reset `Retired` invitation row back to `Pending` without checking the row's current state, which defeats the re-invite the resurrect reset is meant to trigger."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":5,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:1790","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:1790 \u2014 The resurrect op key embeds `replace`, which is re-read from threads on every execution, so after an outcome-unknown attempt a retry with a different `replace` submits a second ResurrectSeat under a new key, while the earlier intent with the stale `replace` is replayed blindly first by `replay_pending`; the two run in an order and against a pane state graph never re-validated."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":6,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/herdr/client.rs:621","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/herdr/client.rs:621 \u2014 The new `agent_name_taken` retry in `HerdrClient::start_agent` can turn a self-collision (an earlier start for the same pane that did go through but whose response was lost) into a second `agent.start` under the pane-qualified name on the same pane."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":7,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/adapter.rs:481","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/adapter.rs:481 \u2014 restore() discards the error from forget_completed, so a failed forget leaves the refusal cached and replayed under the same op key on every retry with nothing logged."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":8,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:1919","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:1919 \u2014 A definitive refusal of the restart rebind (threads.rebind_held_seat) is returned as ExecOutcome::Done, so the effect row reads Done with no error, no attention item and no eprintln; the refusal reason only reaches journal meta."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":9,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:1841","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:1841 \u2014 A Restore whose resurrect keeps returning NotFound, or keeps returning a retryable refusal (ServiceBusy, StaleHostObservation, Unreachable, OutcomeUnknown), stalls with no clones status row and no doctor finding: neither branch writes last_refusal or resurrect_refused meta, and both rows depend on one of those."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":10,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/daemon/clone_status.rs:93","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/daemon/clone_status.rs:93 \u2014 The clones.restart_held row, and so the doctor `restart held` finding, is emitted only for a seat whose fact was freshly read Unresolved after the incarnation change. A seat that graph never re-reads after a Herdr restart, for example because threads is unreachable, gets no row, although design \u00a74.5 lists `never attempted because threads was unreachable` as a case the row covers."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":11,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/daemon/clone_status.rs:75","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/daemon/clone_status.rs:75 \u2014 The `restart_held` status row and doctor finding do not check that the clone's recorded pane still exists. A seated clone whose pane vanished in the restart gets a `restart_held` row (alongside `resume_blocked`) whose remedy tells the operator to rebind onto a pane that no longer exists, or onto the literal pane \"unknown\" when the binding was cleared."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":12,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] CHANGELOG.md:22","text":"[suggested Should-fix] CHANGELOG.md:22 \u2014 The CHANGELOG states unconditionally that an undo-restored seat whose agent exits now gets the ordinary exited-agent relaunch, but the fix only skips the launch record for keyless clones; a keyed undo-restored clone still records `launched:` and so remains excluded from start_needed."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":13,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:1866","text":"[suggested Should-fix] src/threads/effects.rs:1866 \u2014 The resurrect paths write two stores without a shared transaction: the refusal path does `meta_set(resurrect_refused:<clone>)` in the journal and then a separate tree write via `record_refusal` whose error is discarded, and the success/ack paths admit the tree transition and then `let _ = meta_delete(...)`. A crash or error between the two leaves the journal meta and the clone record disagreeing."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":14,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart/profile-9b510293-b854-4149-b916-64e7b38c421d.json:10","text":"[suggested Should-fix] docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart/profile-9b510293-b854-4149-b916-64e7b38c421d.json:10 \u2014 The diff commits a run profile to a public GitHub repository that records about 164 absolute local paths, the OS username and the agent session id, including paths to the full session transcripts under the user's home directory."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":15,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/support/threads_bin.rs:98","text":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/support/threads_bin.rs:98 \u2014 The five new tier-5 tests in threads_real depend on an HG_TEST_THREADS_SUPPORT_BINARY env input that the Herdr release matrix runner never supplies, so under that runner every one of them panics instead of running."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":16,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/e2e_private_herdr.rs:3768","text":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/e2e_private_herdr.rs:3768 \u2014 The four new e2e_private_herdr tests are not in the release matrix's exact-match e2e inventory, which matched every base #[test] before this diff, so the matrix's e2e suite now fails classification for every Herdr version."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":17,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/threads_real.rs:841","text":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/threads_real.rs:841 \u2014 Tier5::new builds graph's production threads ports inside the test process, and Endpoint::from_env there reads the test process's ambient HERDR_GRAPH_THREADS_SOCKET/HERDR_GRAPH_THREADS_INSTANCE, which take precedence over the private env_state_dir; nothing checks the discovered socket against the private root."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":18,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/e2e_private_herdr.rs:3828","text":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/e2e_private_herdr.rs:3828 \u2014 late_rebind_binds_the_fresh_agent_at_its_next_prompt accepts both rebind orders and only proves the late-path escalation inside `if late`, so it can pass without exercising the behavior it is named for."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":19,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/adopt_private_herdr.rs:1077","text":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/adopt_private_herdr.rs:1077 \u2014 close_restart_then_undo_resurrects_the_seat never waits for graph to observe the Herdr restart: its \"graph to answer after the restart\" wait is met by the graph daemon, which never went down, and `settle()` (1.5 s with no commits) can return inside graph's 5 s resubscribe backoff. The \"still closed after the restart\" assertions and the undo can therefore run against the pre-restart incarnation."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":20,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/integration_sweep.rs:3316","text":"[suggested Should-fix] tests/integration_sweep.rs:3316 \u2014 In the after-7d window of keyless_close_then_undo, the `call_count(\"resurrect_seat\") == 0` check is sampled at the first moment the clone shows a reopened pane, before the pass that would issue a ResurrectSeat, so the test passes even if graph resurrects on a stale reversible fact."},{"section":"Not verified (beyond panel cap)","position":21,"key":"[suggested Should-fix] docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart/run.md:53","text":"[suggested Should-fix] docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart/run.md:53 \u2014 The PR head carries its own final review whose recorded verdict is 'not ready' with unresolved must-fix items, so the branch is being presented for review in a state its own process says is not landable."},{"section":"Beyond remainder cap (count only)","position":1,"key":"44 candidates dropped by the remainder cap","text":"44 candidates dropped by the remainder cap \u2014 raise config.remainderCap and re-run to see them"},{"section":"Rejected (with reason)","position":1,"key":"src/threads/effects.rs:1919","text":"src/threads/effects.rs:1919 \u2014 Rebind NotFound is recorded as a definitive refusal for the whole incarnation, contradicting design 4.2 and leaving the seat unbound if threads answers NotFound transiently before its restore hold is in place.\n  reason: 3/3 REJECT. The threads U2 design (herdr-threads docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-26-service-restore-held-seat-design.md, D2/D3/D5) answers the pre-hold window with ServiceBusy (retryable), not NotFound. NotFound is reserved for definitive cases, so recording `rebind_refused` once per incarnation matches design 4.2. The already-placed case returns SeatAlreadyResolved, which the code maps to Done. Design 4.2's \"NotFound ... already placed\" wording is stale prose only."},{"section":"Rejected (with reason)","position":2,"key":"src/threads/effects.rs:1907","text":"src/threads/effects.rs:1907 \u2014 The restart rebind uses one threads op key per incarnation (`rebind:<clone>:<changed_at>`), so if the seat turns Unresolved a second time in the same incarnation after an earlier rebind succeeded, the retry gets threads' stored success replayed under that key and graph records Done without the seat being placed.\n  reason: 2 REJECT, 1 CONFIRM at Nit. Design section 4 states the choice: \"one op key per incarnation, so a want is re-planned, not duplicated\". The scenario needs a seat to be rebound and then read Unresolved again inside the same Herdr incarnation; no mechanism for that was shown, and a restart changes the key. The ground seat's CONFIRM cites herdr-threads docs/design/graph-system-identity/design.md:69 for the replay behaviour, which the majority does not dispute; it concedes the same reachability limit and the 4.5 `restart_held` backstop. The majority evidence answers the dissent, so the default stands. Residual: a key-design nit (add a discriminator such as the fact `read_at`)."},{"section":"Rejected (with reason)","position":3,"key":"src/threads/effects.rs:1798; src/threads/effects.rs:1802","text":"src/threads/effects.rs:1798; src/threads/effects.rs:1802 \u2014 A definitively refused resurrect is re-asked only when replace or the pane changes, not when the seat fact changes or after any time-out, so the undo's restore launch stays blocked indefinitely after the refusal's cause clears.\n  reason: 3/3 REJECT. Design section 3 says a definitive refusal is recorded once and the want is re-planned when its inputs change. The want is keyed by (seat, pane, epoch) and the executor returns Obsolete when `resurrectable()` no longer matches, so a changed fact is covered; `replace` and pane are compared directly. The design states no time-based retry and names the operator remedy via `clones.resurrect_held` after the 90 s grace. The transient-local-error part of this claim is the confirmed finding at src/ports/threads.rs:179."},{"section":"Rejected (with reason)","position":4,"key":"src/threads/adapter.rs:62; src/threads/adapter.rs:792; src/threads/adapter.rs:801","text":"src/threads/adapter.rs:62; src/threads/adapter.rs:792; src/threads/adapter.rs:801 \u2014 Graph registers only service_session_v4 with no v3 or Notify fallback, so against an older threads daemon every threads operation (including summarizer delivery) hard-fails, and the resulting terminal Failed effects are not re-attempted after the daemon is upgraded.\n  reason: 3/3 REJECT. Design line 63: \"An older daemon refuses the v4 registration, and graph's existing registration-failure path reports it (no silent fallback to v3).\" CHANGELOG Migration says \"Upgrade herdr-threads first\" and doctor names the upgrade step. Removing the Notify degrade follows from that stated choice. Terminal Failed rows not being re-attempted is the same Rejected-to-Failed behaviour base had below the v3 floor."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":1,"key":"src/undo/preview.rs:486","text":"src/undo/preview.rs:486 \u2014 The undo-preview window note returns nothing for any fact that reads `keyed: true`. Because `keyed` defaults to true for legacy facts, a keyless clone whose retire-time fact was written before this change and reads `Retired{reversible:false}` gets no warning that undo gives the pane a fresh seat and loses memberships graph does not own.\n  spot check: CONFIRM at Nit. `seat_window_note` matches `Retired { keyed: true, .. } => return None` before the `reversible: false` arm, and legacy facts deserialize as keyed:true. Same root cause as the confirmed finding at src/model/clone.rs:100."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":2,"key":"tests/e2e_private_herdr.rs:3784","text":"tests/e2e_private_herdr.rs:3784 \u2014 The late-rebind test's fixed 95 s sleep leaves about 5 s of margin over the 90 s grace, which graph's own incarnation record can lag by the resubscribe backoff, so the test may quietly take the non-late order.\n  spot check: CONFIRM at Nit. The grace is measured from graph's journalled `incarnation:changed_at`, and src/observe/step.rs:1056 has a 5 s resubscribe sleep. The final assertions are order-independent, so a non-late run still verifies the end state."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":3,"key":"src/reconcile/tests.rs:3919","text":"src/reconcile/tests.rs:3919 \u2014 restart_arm_needs_an_earlier_agent now asserts the opposite of its name: a clone with only a `launched:` meta and no session is relaunched. The original invariant, that the resume rule does not launch a seated clone that never had an agent, now has only shell-harness or keyless coverage.\n  spot check: REJECT. The change is intended (spec 4.3: a `launched:` meta counts as had-agent). The never-launched path is still covered by the `Had::Nothing` arm in src/reconcile/tests.rs (~5497-5534). What remains is a stale test name."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":4,"key":"src/reconcile/herdr_exec.rs:38","text":"src/reconcile/herdr_exec.rs:38 \u2014 The keyless fresh-start gate and the restart_covered change alter agent launch behavior after every Herdr restart with no flag: fresh keyless starts are now delayed up to the 90 s grace, and clones with only a `launched:` meta (never observed with an agent) are now relaunched by the restart rule.\n  spot check: REJECT. Both behaviours are stated design: section 4 \"Gate\" and \"Accepted behaviour\" bound the wait at the 90 s grace, and section 4.3 states the `launched:` rule."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":5,"key":"CHANGELOG.md:29","text":"CHANGELOG.md:29 \u2014 During the documented skew window (threads 3.6.0 daemon, old graph still running), the old graph sees keyless pane closes as reversible retirements and its unretire want issues UnretireSeat for keyless seats on undo, a combination the diff does not test or document.\n  spot check: REJECT. Design line 37 already documents this degradation, and the behaviour lives in the base graph binary, not in this diff. The claim is external and the single spot seat did not mark it UNVERIFIED."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":6,"key":"src/threads/effects.rs:1841","text":"src/threads/effects.rs:1841 \u2014 A resurrect refused as NotFound returns Deferred and records no meta, so every reconcile step until the next seat read changes the fact re-issues a full durable ResurrectSeat mutation: a ResolveSeat RPC, the intent-journal write, the daemon call and forget_completed.\n  spot check: REJECT. Design (resurrect outcomes, ~line 80): \"NotFound: deferred. The next fact read picks the row\". Writing no meta for NotFound is deliberate."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":7,"key":"src/daemon/clone_status.rs:75; src/daemon/clone_status.rs:83","text":"src/daemon/clone_status.rs:75; src/daemon/clone_status.rs:83 \u2014 The restart_held row uses the fixed SEAT_LOST_AFTER (90 s) while the gate it describes uses the configurable relaunch_grace, and the tests hardcode 89/91 s for both so drift goes undetected.\n  spot check: REJECT. `relaunch_grace` has no config-file or CLI source; production uses 90 s for both. The design says \"no new grace constant is added\"."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":8,"key":"src/daemon/clone_status.rs:102","text":"src/daemon/clone_status.rs:102 \u2014 The restart_held and resurrect_held remedies can contain the literal `--pane unknown`, which produces a pasteable operator command that cannot work.\n  spot check: REJECT. Matches the base convention (`key_conflicts` already emits pane \"unknown\"), and the row carries `\"pane\":\"unknown\"` plus a reason."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":9,"key":"src/daemon/clone_status.rs:66","text":"src/daemon/clone_status.rs:66 \u2014 The doctor and status remedy strings put the seat id and pane id into a shell command line without quoting, and an operator is meant to copy and run that line.\n  spot check: REJECT. Seat ids are threads-minted and pane ids Herdr-generated; no user-chosen string reaches these fields, and graph does not execute the printed remedy."},{"section":"Unverified nits (spot-checked)","position":10,"key":"src/threads/adapter.rs:1045","text":"src/threads/adapter.rs:1045 \u2014 When the daemon is older than 3.6.0, every resurrect and rebind is classified as the refusal `Unsupported`. The resulting resurrect_held and restart_held rows tell the operator to run a manual `herdr-threads human seat rebind` rather than to upgrade the daemon; the upgrade hint appears only in the separate `threads` doctor check, and only through a substring match.\n  spot check: REJECT. The design lists Unsupported among definitive refusals surfaced by `resurrect_held`; src/daemon/doctor.rs:112 emits the upgrade finding and service_tests.rs:669-706 tests its wording."},{"section":"Escalations (need human)","position":1,"key":"src/threads/effects.rs:552","text":"src/threads/effects.rs:552 \u2014 The restart rebind is only wanted when the clone's last recorded `runtime.bound` pane id is present in the post-restart snapshot. On a cold restart that renumbers pane ids, a held seated clone gets no rebind and falls through to `restart_held`/operator action. That would fail B2 for that restart shape.\n  reason: UNVERIFIED external (reproduce seat UNVERIFIED; refute and ground REJECT). Open fact: whether a real Herdr restart ever renumbers pane ids. In-repo evidence says no: docs/herdr-spikes.md Spike 3 records \"pane ids reused: yes (w1:p1..p4)\" and the tier-3 tests assert `starts[1].0 == pane`. The reproduce seat notes the spike words it as luck, not a guarantee, and found no authoritative Herdr source. Cheapest check: read the Herdr source for pane id assignment on session restore, or cold-restart a private rig several times after closing a pane and compare ids."},{"section":"Escalations (need human)","position":2,"key":"src/threads/effects.rs:636","text":"src/threads/effects.rs:636 \u2014 A keyless pending Restore whose seat reads `Unresolved` on a verified pane is acknowledged by the succession path, with no resurrect and no rebind. That acknowledgement is written as `AcknowledgeResurrected`, which resets ordinary invitations even though the seat was never brought back.\n  reason: UNVERIFIED external (ground seat UNVERIFIED; reproduce and refute REJECT). Pre-existing on base: 60e287aa src/threads/effects.rs:553 (the `F::Unresolved` acknowledge arm is unchanged), so FYI at most. Open fact: whether threads 3.6.0 can report a just-closed keyless seat as Unresolved before Retired. The ground seat read store/seats/observation.rs and could not rule out an unresolved-then-retired sequence. Cheapest check: on a private Herdr, close an adopted keyless tab, undo at once, and read the seat fact stream for an Unresolved sample before `Retired{reversible}`."}]}
